<p>The generated files have to live in an extension Drupal knows about. The plugin therefore creates a hidden theme in <code>dist/</code> called <code>&lt;theme&gt;_dist</code>, and your theme uses it as base theme.</p>

<h2>Generated for this theme</h2>
{% include code_block with { lang: 'yaml', title: generated.info.path, code: generated.info.code } only %}

<p>Your theme only has to point to it:</p>
{% embed code_block with { lang: 'yaml', title: 'uebertool_docs.info.yml' } %}{% block code %}{% verbatim %}
name: 'UEBERTOOL Docs'
type: theme
base theme: uebertool_docs_dist
core_version_requirement: ^11
{% endverbatim %}{% endblock %}{% endembed %}

<h2>What it contains</h2>
<ul>
  <li><strong>Global libraries:</strong> <code>css__tailwind</code>, <code>js__main</code> and <code>css__gin-custom</code> are attached on every page.</li>
  <li><strong>Base theme:</strong> the dist theme itself extends <code>stable9</code>. Change it with the <code>baseTheme</code> option.</li>
  <li><strong>Package:</strong> the theme name, or the <code>themePackage</code> option.</li>
  <li><strong>Hidden:</strong> it never shows up in the Appearance UI.</li>
</ul>

{% embed aside %}
  {% block content %}
    <p>The dist theme is written on <code>vite build</code> and when the dev server starts. Run one of them before enabling your theme for the first time, otherwise Drupal cannot find the base theme.</p>
  {% endblock %}
{% endembed %}
